<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπομφάλιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽὀμφαλόσ̓</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on the navel</i> or
				<i>central point,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλεν δεινὸν σάκος..μέσσον ἐ.</span>
			<i>in the centre, on the boss</i> of the shield, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.267
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῦκον ἐ.</span> a fig <i>with
				a navel-like stalk,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.22
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Zon.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπομφάλιον, τό,</span>
			<i>the umbilical region,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Parth.
				35.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.169
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>plaster applied to the navel,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καθαρτικά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aët.
					3.135
				</span></i>
			, cf. Philum.ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.25
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
